<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nizari–Musta'li schism</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1094</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as 1094 succession crisis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nizari-ismailism">Nizari</a>–Musta'li schism was the division of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ismailism">Ismaili</a> Shi'a community following a succession crisis in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimid Caliphate</a> in 1094. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-afdal">al-Afdal</a> bypassed the designated heir Nizar in favour of al-Musta'li, and the Nizari faction broke away. The split destroyed the universal authority of the Fatimid missionary organisation and weakened the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphate</a>.</p></div>
